{
  "manufacturer": "Teracom",
  "manufacturer_slug": "teracom",
  "model": "TSV300 AC/DC voltage transducer with Modbus RTU",
  "model_slug": "tsv300",
  "short_model": "TSV300",
  "aliases": [
    "TSV300"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Sensor (AC/DC voltage transducer)",
  "applies_to": "TSV300 per the Teracom TSV300 user manual Revision R1.4, firmware V1.06 or later.",
  "summary": "The TSV300 is a Teracom 4-channel true-RMS voltage transducer (0-264 VAC or up to 370 VDC) with Modbus RTU over RS-485. It gives AC and DC readings with min/max as 32-bit floats and as 32-bit signed integers x1000.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The register table prints both a PDU (wire) address and a logical address (PDU + 40001 for holding registers). 'documented' holds the logical number; the PDU number is what goes in the request, e.g. logical 40101 = PDU 100."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "V1.06 or later",
  "source": {
    "title": "TSV300 User manual",
    "doc_number": "Revision R1.4",
    "revision_date": "2026-10",
    "url": "https://www.teracomsystems.com/download/tsv300-ac-voltage-transducer-with-modbus-rtu-interface/",
    "pages": "pp. 5-7 (Modbus address table)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Addresses are taken from the manual's PDU address column (0-based); the logical column is the same number plus 40001, the holding-register offset the manual states.",
    "All 32-bit values follow the Data order register (PDU 13): 1 = most significant word first (factory default), 2 = least significant word first. The map shows the default, ABCD.",
    "Left out: the 32-bit float/integer test-value registers (PDU 82-95), which only exist to check word order; the 16-bit test values are kept.",
    "AC blocks start at PDU 100 (float) and 150 (x1000 int32); DC blocks at PDU 500 and 550. Min/max registers start as NaN after a reset and track readings from then on.",
    "A missing reading returns NaN (float) or -2147483648 (int32).",
    "The manual lists function codes 3 and 6 for the float multiplier/offset registers; a 2-register write normally needs function 16."
  ],
